1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,360
A sausage floating between two fingers?

2
00:00:05,410 --> 00:00:07,130
Touch the tips of your index fingers
a hand-span in front of your eyes

3
00:00:07,180 --> 00:00:09,080
Don't look at your fingers —
look at a far wall

4
00:00:09,130 --> 00:00:12,430
Now pull them slightly apart…

5
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:16,200
Try it now!
Eyes on something far away

6
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:19,200
What's floating
between your fingers?

7
00:00:19,250 --> 00:00:23,200
Pull them further apart
and the sausage shrinks

8
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:26,770
A finger sausage floating in the air!

9
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:28,840
Seen from above,
your two eyes are a little apart

10
00:00:28,890 --> 00:00:33,510
When you look far away, your close fingers
show up in a different place for each eye

11
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:35,080
The left eye's picture and the right eye's picture…

12
00:00:35,130 --> 00:00:36,580
When your brain overlaps them into one

13
00:00:36,630 --> 00:00:38,750
Where the two fingertips overlap = the sausage!

14
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:41,520
Close one eye?
There's nothing to overlap, so it disappears

15
00:00:41,570 --> 00:00:45,090
Overlapping two pictures like this
is how you tell near from far

16
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:47,140
This is called "stereo vision"

17
00:00:47,190 --> 00:00:49,640
NEXT: Your eyes have a boss too?
